      "text": [
        ":\nكَتَبْتُ إِلَى صَاحِبِ اَلدَّارِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ وُلِدَ لِي مَوْلُودٌ وَ حَلَقْتُ رَأْسَهُ وَ وَزَنْتُ شَعْرَهُ بِالدَّرَاهِمِ وَ تَصَدَّقْتُ بِهِ قَالَ \"لاَ يَجُوزُ وَزْنُهُ إِلاَّ بِالذَّهَبِ أَوِ اَلْفِضَّةِ وَ كَذَا جَرَتِ اَلسُّنَّةُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4727 - It was narrated from Harun ibn Muslim who said:\nI wrote to the 'Sahib al-Dar' (Master of the House Imam Muhammad ibn Hassan Al-Mahdi (as)) saying: \"A child was born to me, and I shaved his head, weighed his hair in dirhams, and gave its equivalent in charity.\"\nImam (as) replied: \"It is not permissible to weigh it except with gold or silver, and this is the established Sunnah.\""
        ]
      }
